    "question": {
      ":question/id": "35b6907e-43ed-5087-8f19-2c1743bbd9fc",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{\\prime}$ given that $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨\\ln{(t )},\\,t^{3},\\,t⟩$ and $v(t)=3 t.$ Assume $t>0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{\\prime}=v(t)\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)+v^{\\prime}(t)\\mathbf{f}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\ln{(t )})=\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})=3 t^{2} \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,3 t^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\ v^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(3 t)⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,3 t^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,9 t^{3},\\,3 t⟩ \\\\ P_2 & =(3)⟨\\ln{(t )},\\,t^{3},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 \\ln{(t )},\\,3 t^{3},\\,3 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{\\prime} & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =⟨3 \\ln{(t )} + 3,\\,12 t^{3},\\,6 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
